  \\\\\n&= (x - 5)(x - 2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3\\left(x^2-7x+10\\right) \\\\[5pt] &= 3(x-5)(x-2) \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535344 17592186045417 false] [17592186175725 1074 "First, notice that we can factor out a $3$ from each of the terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-21x+30 & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}-7x+10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to factor the polynomial $x^2-7x+10$ in parentheses.\n\nWe start by listing the factor pairs of the constant term $(10),$ but only the negative factor pairs since the coefficient of the linear term $(-7)$ is negative.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1,-10),\\,(-2,-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $(-7)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)+(-10) & =-11 & \\times  \\\\ (-2)+(-5) & =-7 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the factor pair identified above, we write the linear term as $-7x=-2x-5x,$ and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-7x+10 & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x-5x+10 & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+(-5x+10) & = \\\\ x(x-2)-5(x-2) & = \\\\ (x-5)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n3\\left(x^2-7x+10\\right)&=\\[5pt]\n3(x-5)(x-2)\n\t}\n$$" 13194139535344 17592186045417 true] [17592186175745 1071 "The concentration of a solution, measured in moles per liter $(\\textrm{mol}/\\textrm{L})$, varies inversely with the volume of the solution, measured in liters $(\\textrm{L})$. When the volume of the solution is $0.25\\,\\text{L}$, the concentration is $2 \\,\\textrm{mol}/\\textrm{L}$. Find the concentration when the volume of the solution is $8\\,\\textrm{L}$." 13194139535344 17592186045417 false] [17592186175745 1071 "The concentration of a solution, measured in moles per liter $(\\textrm{mol}/\\textrm{L}),$ varies inversely with the volume of the solution, measured in liters $(\\textrm{L}).$ When the volume of the solution is $0.25\\,\\t